  "description": "Z-29s-a: one signal series reduced onto the dates of a sampled price series. Read by pytest (test_signal_aggregation.py: sample_signal_series, backend/app/services/signals/aggregation.py, on every case) and by Vitest (timeSeriesAggregation.test.ts: downsampleRenderedSignal on the browser_parity cases, each run of a line or area downsampled alone as backendRenderer.ts splits it, the expected split at its markers). render_dates: the sampled price dates, ascending, one per bucket: the last day of each ISO week (Monday to Sunday) or calendar month, the last one cut at the range's end, as price_sampling.sample_dates gives them; daily, every day. points: the daily series as a plugin sends it, nulls included (a band: lower, middle, upper). expected: the reduced points, each gap marker {date, value: null} included. browser_parity false only for a residue of the contract (R1, R3) or a synthetic input, said in its note. series_sets (O1, Z-29b prelude): the series of one signal reduced each alone on the same render_dates, then aligned: every series carries the union of the dates the reductions left, a point without a value (a band: lower, middle and upper null) where a series has none. Per series, points are the daily series as a plugin sends it and expected the aligned reduction; read by pytest (align_signal_series) and by Vitest, which draws each series alone as it does a case. browser_parity false for R5.",
